          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A patient from South India who regularly bathes in stagnant pond water presents with a nasal polyp that has a characteristic strawberry surface studded with white sporangia. What is the most likely diagnosis?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Lupus vulgaris (nasal tuberculosis)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Lupus vulgaris presents with apple-jelly nodules at the nasal tip and caseating granulomas on histology. The Ziehl-Neelsen stain is positive for acid-fast bacilli. A strawberry polyp with sporangia points to rhinosporidiosis.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Rhinosporidiosis</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Rhinosporidiosis is endemic in South India, linked to bathing in ponds and rivers. The pathognomonic finding is a strawberry-surfaced polyp studded with white sporangia, confirmed by PAS staining on histology.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Rhinoscleroma</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Rhinoscleroma is caused by Klebsiella rhinoscleromatis and shows two pathognomonic biopsy features — Mikulicz cells and Russell bodies — not a strawberry polyp with sporangia.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Granulomatosis with polyangiitis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>GPA is a necrotising vasculitis involving the kidneys and lungs, diagnosed by c-ANCA positivity. It does not produce a strawberry polyp with sporangia.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The strawberry-surfaced polyp with white sporangia, in a patient from South India with pond-water exposure, is the hallmark of rhinosporidiosis. Each granulomatous nasal disease has distinctive morphological and geographic markers that separate it from the others."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. The combination of South Indian endemicity, pond-water exposure, and a strawberry polyp with white sporangia is virtually diagnostic of rhinosporidiosis."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
